Parked 2026-09-24 -- prepared and validated, but out of the queue.

WHY: at 863 mM residues this is 2x the concentration at which md_full
vitrified (406 mM: width 14.2 +/- 0.00 nm over 2 us, chain-order correlation
0.982, ~1020 mg/mL, zero beads in the dilute phase). It would almost certainly
return TRAPPED -- ~11 GPU-hours for an answer we can already predict -- and its
dilute region is only ~2x the dense-slab thickness, so it could not give a
trustworthy c_sat even if it did condense.

Parked to let ladder/md_full_lowc run sooner; that one is a genuine control
(is md_full more cohesive, or just more concentrated?) rather than a
near-certain negative.

Run it if the lower rungs turn out interesting -- e.g. if fl_c4x (431 mM) comes
back liquid rather than trapped, the jamming threshold is higher than expected
and 863 mM becomes worth measuring. If you do, widen the box first so the
dilute region is >3x the slab thickness.

To un-park:  rm ladder/fl_c8x/.parked
